Always write clean, readable code
Use comments to explain what code does
Prefer simple solutions over complex ones

## Project directory structure

Keep this tree in sync with the repo. When you add, remove, or rename top-level items, week folders, or other tracked project files, update this section in the same edit (or immediately after).

```
hcde530code/
├── .cursorrules          # Pointer: see week2/.cursorrules when workspace is repo root
├── README.md
├── week2.md              # A2-style competency write-up (also see week2/week2.md for long form)
└── week2/
    ├── .cursorrules          # Cursor / AI project rules (this file)
    ├── PROJECT_CONTEXT.md    # Who this is for, constraints, assistant tone
    ├── .gitignore
    ├── app_reviews.csv
    ├── app_review_summary.py
    ├── clean_responses.py
    ├── count_roles.py
    ├── demo_responses.csv
    ├── demo_word_count.py
    ├── responses.csv           # sample input for clean_responses.py
    └── week2.md              # Week 2 reflection: Competency 2
```

Notes:
- `week2/` is also its own Git repository (nested `.git`); the repo root may be a separate Git repo—respect whichever root the user is working in.
